{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_0161fApgnk5XoMSNGMYtAHqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **Q4: Cost and capacity planning for LLM app at scale** (`answers/07-004-cost-and-capacity-planning-for-llm-app-at-scale.md`).\n\nKey content in the note:\n\n- **Cost formula**: `cost/query = (input_tokens × price_in) + (output_tokens × price_out)` — worked through at 1M queries/day with GPT-4o ($10,500/day baseline)\n- **Sensitivity matrix**: QPS × model tier table (GPT-4o / GPT-4o-mini / self-hosted Llama 3 70B) showing cost curves and the break-even point (~$50K/month for self-hosting)\n- **Top cost drivers**: output tokens (3-10× more expensive than input), RAG retrieved context (often the dominant input cost), system prompt at scale\n- **Capacity planning**: peak QPS not average (80% of enterprise traffic in 4 hours = 3× peak), API quota lead time (weeks), 30-40% headroom for burst\n- **Self-hosted sizing**: vLLM PagedAttention 2-3× throughput improvement factored into GPU replica math\n- **4 concrete pitfalls**: using average token counts, planning for average QPS, ignoring output tokens, self-hosting below break-even\n\n13 questions remain in the category (Q5–Q16 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":75758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":293,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06c47032-aafb-461b-bc83-b56d9c52f623","uuid":"a4708f7a-0b56-4789-a0d8-b21d5703f648"}
